# One-off scratch: benchmarked Bedrock models to pick the one wired into rag.py.
# Kept locally, not part of the deployed app.
backend/compare.py

# Retired code and artifacts -- the LightFM recommender, the clustering
# pipeline, and the Ask index's build scripts (they read LightFM-era outputs) --
# kept on disk, out of the repo. backend/data/index/ (the Ask tab's shipped
# index) stays tracked.
local_archive/
# build_ask_index.py's resumable cache of finished Titan embeddings.
data/ask_embed_cache.jsonl

# pbpstats extension: fetch_pbpstats.py's gzipped API response cache and the
# bulk CSVs it renders from it (~445 MB; pbpstats_lineups.csv alone is 302 MB,
# past GitHub's 100 MB per-file limit). Build-time inputs only — no committed
# artifact depends on them, and re-running fetch_pbpstats.py rebuilds them.
data/pbpstats_raw/
data/pbpstats_lineups.csv
data/pbpstats_players.csv
# lineup_features.py output (~137 MB, rebuilt in under a minute). The crosswalk
# and unmatched report beside it are small and tracked.
data/lineup_panel.csv

# AWS CLI scratch output
/response.json

# Old root-level LightFM / clustering outputs, should any be regenerated from
# local_archive/. backend/data/players.csv (the Ask tab's player table) is tracked.
/models_all.joblib
/interactions.csv
/players.csv
/master_stats.csv
/master_clustered.csv
/master_team_stats.csv
/master_team_clustered.csv
/adv_stats_combined.csv
/per_100_combined.csv
/per_36_combined.csv

# fetch_salaries.py's cache of Basketball-Reference team pages (~800 gzipped
# HTML files). data/salaries.csv and data/team_payroll.csv are rendered from it
# and tracked; --consolidate-only rebuilds them without the network.
data/salaries_raw/
# The retired LightFM recommender's scores, kept locally as an optional
# baseline: evaluate_recs.py / rubric.py read the full dump if present, and
# impact_recs.py --compare its top 10s. Neither can be regenerated any more.
data/lightfm_scores_full.csv
data/recs_lightfm.csv
# fetch_transactions.py's cache of BBRef transaction pages; data/transactions.csv is tracked.
data/transactions_raw/

# impact_recs.py --free-agency output (experimental, opt-in); regenerate when needed.
data/recs_impact_fa.csv
# fetch_wikipedia_fa.py's cache of Wikipedia transaction pages (re-fetching is
# rate-limited); data/wikipedia_fa.csv is rendered from it.
data/wikipedia_raw/
# Regenerated diagnostics / analysis outputs nothing downstream reads:
# lineup_features.py's crosswalk misses and fit_model.py's pooled pair fit
# (impact_recs.py reads data/archetype_main.csv).
data/unmatched_report.csv
data/archetype_fit.csv
# Generated reports nothing reads: impact_recs.py's top 10s (the app serves
# backend/data/recs.csv, from export_recs.py) and contract_status.py's table
# (acquisition.py recomputes it). Rerun the script to get them.
data/recs_impact.csv
data/recs_impact_open.csv
data/contract_status.csv
# Spreadsheet review sheets from audit.py sheet; decisions live in judgments.csv.
data/review/review_*.csv
